-- Every party any instrument here gives a right to or puts a duty on, in
-- one type, so that any two modules can be imported together (MMS-532).
-- Until 2026-10-21 six modules each declared their own `Party`, and the
-- compiler refused to import two of them into one file ("multiple
-- definitions for the identifier Party"), which the one codebase cannot
-- live with (MMS-521). A new party is added here, never declared again.

IMPORT prelude

§ `הצדדים — אוצר מילים משותף לכל המסמכים`

@desc The parties the instruments give rights to or put duties on.
DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    `the teaching employee`
    `the State`
    `the teachers' union`
    `the Ministry of Education`
    `the school principal`
    `the district manager`
    `the teaching personnel division`
    `the steering committee`
    `the supreme follow-up committee`
    `the wages commissioner`
    `the union's secretary-general`
    `the wages commissioner at the Treasury`
    `the principal`
    `the employee's superior`
    `the follow-up committee`
    `the employer`
    `the supervisor`
    `the local authority or owning body`
    `the director-general`
    `the Treasury`
    `the Civil Service Commission`
    `the conditions-of-service department`
    `the parity committee`
    `the district medical committee`
    `the National Insurance Institute`
    `the secondary teachers' organisation`
    `the school management`
    `the Oz evaluation-model committee`
